/*
 * Aggregates all modules involved in the declaration phase of the compilation.
 *
 * The declarator subsystem is responsible for transforming parsed syntax into
 * declared semantic symbols. It performs the first semantic pass of the
 * compiler, building symbol tables, resolving names, and preparing the
 * structures that later validation phases rely on.
 *
 * This module exposes:
 *   - DeclareErrorMessage: error messages specific to the declaration phase,
 *   - Declarator:          the main visitor responsible for symbol declaration.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::declarator
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/declarator.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
